        <!--
          plugin-parser is commented out: it pulls tika-parsers-standard-package 3.2.2, a
          meta artifact bundling the whole Tika stack (POI, PDFBox, BouncyCastle,
          commons-compress) in versions that clash with the rest of the platform. It breaks
          requireUpperBoundDeps on lutece-starter, which is the only module where it meets
          forms-starter and appointment-starter:
            org.apache.pdfbox:xmpbox            2.0.24 (plugin-htmltopdf) vs 3.0.5 here
            org.apache.poi:poi                  5.4.0 (plugin-appointment) vs 5.4.1 here
            org.apache.poi:poi-ooxml            5.4.0 (plugin-appointment) vs 5.4.1 here
            org.apache.commons:commons-compress 1.27.1 (plugin-appointment) vs 1.28.0 here
            org.bouncycastle:bcprov-jdk18on     1.81 vs 1.81.1, both from Tika itself
          The POI, commons-compress and BouncyCastle clashes are plain version bumps and
          could be pinned in dependencyManagement. The PDFBox one cannot: Tika 3.2.2 needs
          PDFBox 3.x, while openhtmltopdf-pdfbox 1.0.10, pulled by plugin-htmltopdf through
          forms-starter, is compiled against the PDFBox 2.x API. Both land on the same
          classpath, where pdfbox resolves to 3.0.5 and xmpbox to 2.0.24, and HTML to PDF
          generation would fail at runtime with NoSuchMethodError. Restore this dependency
          only once plugin-htmltopdf moves to an openhtmltopdf release built on PDFBox 3,
          or once the Tika PDF module is excluded here.
        -->
